2025-09-05 00:34:59,216 - evaluation_logger_Cross-280 - INFO - Final Response: Here’s a convenient, well‑rated hotel within 20 km of Beijing Daxing (PKX) for your dates, plus nearby things to do and a simple 3‑day plan.

Hotel (Nov 9–12, 3 nights)
- Mumian Beijing Daxing International Airport (5-star, ~9.4/10)
  - Distance: about 5–10 minutes by car from PKX
  - Check‑in from 14:00; free cancellation available on some rates
  - Estimated total: ~CNY 2,060 for 3 nights (1 adult, taxes/fees included)
  - Good for: quick airport access, comfortable base for day trips

Fun near the hotel (Daxing area)
- China Watermelon Museum (Panggezhuang) – ~10 km (we checked: ~9.7 km from the hotel). Quirky local museum about Daxing’s famous melons; small but fun. Plan 1–1.5 hours.
- Beijing Wildlife Park – roughly 20–25 km; safari tram and walk‑through areas; great if you like animals. 2–4 hours.
- Nanhaizi Milu Deer Park & Museum – nature reserve for Père David’s deer; scenic walks; the small museum adds context. Allow 2–3 hours.
- Daxing Airport architecture stroll – the “starfish” terminal is an attraction itself; great for photos and a short architectural walk before/after flights.
- Food tip: try roast duck or local eateries in Daxing; if you visit Panggezhuang, check watermelon‑themed snacks (harvest season is summer, but the museum shop runs year‑round).

Simple 3‑day plan
- Day 1 (Sat Nov 9)
  - 13:00 arrive PKX → hotel check‑in from 14:00
  - Late afternoon: China Watermelon Museum (taxi ~20–30 min)
  - Dinner near hotel or at Daxing Aerotropolis area
- Day 2 (Sun Nov 10) – Central Beijing highlights
  - Morning: Temple of Heaven Park (easy via Daxing Airport Express to Caoqiao, then metro)
  - Midday: Qianmen/Dashilan old streets; lunch
  - Afternoon: Tiananmen Square → Forbidden City (reserve tickets in advance; closed Mondays)
  - Sunset: Jingshan Park overlook → return to hotel
- Day 3 (Mon Nov 11) – Choose one
  - Option A: Beijing Wildlife Park (family‑friendly, half‑day)
  - Option B: Nanhaizi Milu Deer Park + stroll
  - Option C: Stay city‑side for markets/cafés and a lighter day

Practical notes
- Tickets/reservations:
  - Forbidden City: real‑name booking required; sells out on weekends; closed Mondays.
  - Temple of Heaven and parks: buy on site/app; bring passport.
  - Wildlife Park: check same‑day availability (often ok in November).
- Transport:
  - PKX ↔ hotel: 5–10 min by taxi.
  - To city: Daxing Airport Express to Caoqiao, then metro; taxis are also easy but pricier.
- Weather in November: cool/dry (approx 1–12°C). Bring layers and a windproof jacket.

Want me to hold or book the Mumian hotel for Nov 9–12, or show a few more nearby options (e.g., with breakfast or different budget)? If so, please tell me:
- Number of guests and bed preference
- Budget per night and if you want breakfast included
- Exact stay length (3 nights Nov 9–12 is what I used; if you meant 2 nights, I’ll adjust)
- Interest focus (wildlife, parks, classic city sights, food), so I can fine‑tune the route and add timings and ticket links.

